{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c841","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06ee5-ad0e-7750-9534-32e3571b58b2"},"sequence":635,"recorded_at":1780531400001265,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"268a8b73-3d5a-46cf-996a-bd1fafa2d2a2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"268a8b73-3d5a-46cf-996a-bd1fafa2d2a2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"268a8b73-3d5a-46cf-996a-bd1fafa2d2a2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"b230d22b-d015-4911-becc-11df90b83d51"},"task_id":"b230d22b-d015-4911-becc-11df90b83d51","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"b230d22b-d015-4911-becc-11df90b83d51","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-13-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"type Error\\\\|Detail\\\\|func errorCode\\\\|func Is\\\" internal/terminalbackend/terminalbackend.go | head -n 20\\ngrep -n \\\"func parseKind\\\\|func needsDigest\\\\|func ParseID\\\\|maxProtocolVersions\\\\|maxGenerationBytes\\\" internal/terminalbackend/*.go | head\\nsed -n '1960,2000p' README.md\\nls internal/traceability/ 2>/dev/null && head -c 2000 internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json\",\n  \"description\": \"Check Error type, README, traceability\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"82:// BackendID names the identity at issue when there is one. Detail is a static\\n84:type Error struct {\\n87:\\tDetail    string\\n92:\\t\\treturn \\\"terminal backend refused: \\\" + err.Code + \\\" at \\\" + err.Detail\\n94:\\treturn \\\"terminal backend refused: \\\" + err.Code + \\\" for \\\" + err.BackendID + \\\" at \\\" + err.Detail\\n98:func errorCode(err error, code string) bool {\\n107:func IsNotFound(err error) bool { return errorCode(err, CodeNotFound) }\\n110:func IsAmbiguous(err error) bool { return errorCode(err, CodeAmbiguous) }\\n113:func IsUntrusted(err error) bool { return errorCode(err, CodeUntrusted) }\\n116:func IsDrift(err error) bool { return errorCode(err, CodeDrift) }\\n119:func IsRestoreMismatch(err error) bool { return errorCode(err, CodeRestoreMismatch) }\\n122:func IsStaleGeneration(err error) bool { return errorCode(err, CodeStaleGeneration) }\\n130:\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", &Error{Code: CodeNotFound, Detail: \\\"terminal_backend_id bound\\\"}\\n133:\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", &Error{Code: CodeNotFound, BackendID: value, Detail: \\\"terminal_backend_id grammar\\\"}\\n136:\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", &Error{Code: CodeNotFound, BackendID: value, Detail: \\\"terminal_backend_id reserved namespace\\\"}\\n167:\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", &Error{Code: CodeNotFound, Detail: \\\"implementation_kind vocabulary\\\"}\\n207:\\t\\treturn &Error{Code: CodeDrift, BackendID: record.ID, Detail: \\\"implementation_version semver\\\"}\\n213:\\t\\treturn &Error{Code: CodeNotFound, BackendID: record.ID, Detail: err.Error()}\\n217:\\t\\t\\treturn &Error{Code: CodeUntrusted, BackendID: record.ID, Detail: \\\"executable_digest\\\"}\\n220:\\t\\treturn &Error{Code: CodeDrift, BackendID: record.ID, Detail: \\\"executable_digest must be null\\\"}\\ninternal/terminalbackend/manifest.go:914:\\tif len(versions) < 1 || len(versions) > maxProtocolVersions {\\ninternal/terminalbackend/manifest.go:1330:\\tif !utf8.ValidString(rawGeneration) || len(rawGeneration) < 1 || len(rawGeneration) > maxGenerationBytes {\\ninternal/terminalbackend/terminalbackend.go:68:// maxGenerationBytes is the Section 4.B/7.A bound: string[1..256].\\ninternal/terminalbackend/terminalbackend.go:69:const maxGenerationBytes = 256\\ninternal/terminalbackend/terminalbackend.go:71:// maxProtocolVersions is the Section 4.B bound: sorted unique semver[1..32].\\ninternal/terminalbackend/terminalbackend.go:72:const maxProtocolVersions = 32\\ninternal/terminalbackend/terminalbackend.go:128:func ParseID(value string) (string, error) {\\ninternal/terminalbackend/terminalbackend.go:162:func parseKind(value string) (Kind, error) {\\ninternal/terminalbackend/terminalbackend.go:173:func needsDigest(kind Kind) bool {\\ninternal/terminalbackend/terminalbackend.go:228:\\tif len(versions) < 1 || len(versions) > maxProtocolVersions {\\n```text\\nsection coverage: bindings=49 full=1 partial=3 sliver=1 unevidenced=41 unmeasured=3 unowned=2 clauses_discharged=17/403\\n```\\n\\nForty-nine section bindings discharge 17 of the 403 normative clauses their\\nsections carry. One binding is `full` (Section 6.2, whose single clause is the\\nnative-Windows `conpty` requirement, discharged by the positive\\n`TestEveryPinnedReaderHasPositiveNativeWindowsAndWSL2Lanes` lanes together\\nwith the negative `TestDecodeRefusesNonConptyBackendOnNativeWindows` legacy\\nrefusal arm), three are\\n`partial` (Section 14.2 at 8/9, bound to\\n[`internal/cliresult`](internal/cliresult), whose undischarged clause `14.2#6`\\nis the process exit status this repository has no binary to produce; and\\nSection 15.1 at 5/7 and Section 15.3 at 2/3, both bound to\\n[`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror); the three undischarged clauses there are\\nthe RPC hello obligation `15.1#5`, the bootstrap-row sentence `15.1#6` that\\nbinds the provider plugin rather than the host, and the hello-key and\\nTerminalBackend-capability prohibition `15.3#3` - this repository builds no RPC\\nhello frame, no provider plugin, and no TerminalBackend capability set), one is\\n`sliver` (Section 10.3, whose chunk offset invariant is\\nenforced by `validateBlobDescriptor` while its two receiver clauses have no\\nimplementation), three are `unmeasured` (Sections 7.3, 13.14.5 and 15.2, each of\\nwhich carries a gap saying why the scanner measures zero and what is missing),\\nand forty-one are `unevidenced`. Two sections are recorded unowned.\\nAssigned-scope admission therefore succeeds today for `-section 6.2` and\\nnothing else; every other assignment is refused with its ratio and its gap.\\nA `partial` binding is refused by assigned-scope admission exactly like an\\n`unevidenced` one: admission requires `full`.\\n\\nOne admitted binding out of forty-nine covers a single clause, and it is\\ndisclosed here rather than hidden: without Section 6.2 the admit path would only\\never be exercised synthetically. Its discharge is no longer positive-only: the\\nnative-Windows lanes carry the positive arm and\\n`TestDecodeRefusesNonConptyBackendOnNativeWindows` the legacy refusal arm,\\nboth registered against the `config-versioned-readers` acceptance case.\\n\\nThat is a disclosure of the shipped state, not a target that was met.\\n`TestRunRefusesEveryAssignedSectionThatOnlySlivers` and\\n`TestVerifyAssignedSectionsRefusesEveryBindingThatOnlySlivers` pin every failing\\nbinding with its exact measured ratio, so a section that becomes covered has to\\nleave those tables deliberately. Five further gaps the disclosure surfaced:\\ncmd\\nownership.v0.5.0.json\\nreadme_figures_pin_test.go\\ntraceability_test.go\\ntraceability.go\\n{\\n  \\\"format\\\": \\\"ax-spec-to-code-ownership\\\",\\n  \\\"format_version\\\": 1,\\n  \\\"source\\\": {\\n    \\\"repository\\\": \\\"relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec\\\",\\n    \\\"release\\\": \\\"v0.5.0\\\",\\n    \\\"commit\\\": \\\"28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c\\\",\\n    \\\"document_path\\\": \\\"SPEC.md\\\",\\n    \\\"document_sha256\\\": \\\"562546d240f0fa3e71b47e6359a002f9892c0efd97e19eb55917527552ac484a\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"source-pin-exact\\\",\\n      \\\"production\\\": {\\n        \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/specpin/pin.go\\\",\\n        \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"Current\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"tests\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/specpin/pin_test.go\\\",\\n          \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"TestCurrentPinsPublishedV050Source\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"source-pin-refusal\\\",\\n      \\\"production\\\": {\\n        \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/specpin/pin.go\\\",\\n        \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"Verify\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"tests\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/specpin/pin_test.go\\\",\\n          \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"TestVerifyRejectsIdentityAndContractDrift\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/specpin/pin_test.go\\\",\\n          \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"TestVerifyRejectsPartialMalformedAndByteDifferentReads\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"source-pin-compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"production\\\": {\\n        \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/specpin/pin.go\\\",\\n        \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"ContractsForRelease\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"tests\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/specpin/pin_test.go\\\",\\n          \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"TestContractsForReleasePreservesV043Compatibility\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"source-pin-idempotency-isolation\\\",\\n      \\\"production\\\": {\\n        \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/specpin/pin.go\\\",\\n        \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"Current\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"tests\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/specpin/pin_test.go\\\",\\n          \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"TestCurrentIsIdempotentAndReturnsIsolatedData\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"AC-PATH-001\\\",\\n      \\\"production\\\": {\\n        \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/config/loader.go\\\",\\n        \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"Load\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"tests\\\": [\\n        {\\n \",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 7296,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1824,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
