ile its two receiver clauses have no\n1981|implementation), three are `unmeasured` (Sections 7.3, 13.14.5 and 15.2, each of\n1982|which carries a gap saying why the scanner measures zero and what is missing),\n1983|and forty-one are `unevidenced`. Two sections are recorded unowned.\n1984|Assigned-scope admission therefore succeeds today for `-section 6.2` and\n1985|nothing else; every other assignment is refused with its ratio and its gap.\n1986|A `partial` binding is refused by assigned-scope admission exactly like an\n1987|`unevidenced` one: admission requires `full`.\n1988|\n1989|One admitted binding out of forty-nine covers a single clause, and it is\n1990|disclosed here rather than hidden: without Section 6.2 the admit path would only\n1991|ever be exercised synthetically. Its discharge is no longer positive-only: the\n1992|native-Windows lanes carry the positive arm and\n(more lines below)"}}}
