{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d171","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06ee5-ad0e-7750-9534-32e3571b58b2"},"sequence":1811,"recorded_at":1780531400003617,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"268a8b73-3d5a-46cf-996a-bd1fafa2d2a2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"268a8b73-3d5a-46cf-996a-bd1fafa2d2a2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"268a8b73-3d5a-46cf-996a-bd1fafa2d2a2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"f8258713-127b-4883-81ba-1b1cda1bb327"},"task_id":"f8258713-127b-4883-81ba-1b1cda1bb327","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"f8258713-127b-4883-81ba-1b1cda1bb327","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: line 3263\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-\"gap\": \"Clause 15.3#3 additionally forbids Structured Error from appearing as an RPC hello key or a TerminalBackend capability, and ExitCodeFor resolves a code-to-exit mapping rather than building either advertisement. No RPC hello frame and no TerminalBackend capability set is built anywhere in this repository, so Section 15.3 keeps that clause unimplemented.\",\n+\"gap\": \"Clause 15.3#3 additionally forbids Structured Error from appearing as an RPC hello key or a TerminalBackend capability, and ExitCodeFor resolves a code-to-exit mapping rather than building either advertisement. No RPC hello frame is built anywhere in this repository, and the closed 16-capability admission registry in internal/terminalbackend is never advertised on an RPC hello path and carries no Structured Error code, so Section 15.3 keeps that clause unimplemented.\",\n"}}}
